<section class="inner-sec">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">How it works in a clinic</div>
  <h2>Every referral booked, every plan finished</h2>
  <p class="lede">One receptionist covers the phone, the texts and the website — getting new patients scheduled quickly and keeping existing ones on the calendar, while your therapists stay in treatment.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Missed-call text-back</strong>A call your desk couldn't reach becomes a text conversation in seconds, instead of a voicemail cleared at the end of the day.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Books new referrals fast</strong>New patients get scheduled the same day they call rather than waiting on a callback — the single biggest reason referrals leak to another clinic.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Answers the referral question</strong>Whether a referral is needed, what to bring, what the first visit involves, how long sessions run — answered from what you've published, any hour.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Keeps the plan on track</strong>Reminders and easy rescheduling by text, so a missed visit becomes a moved visit instead of the moment someone quietly stops coming.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Fills cancellations</strong>When a slot opens, it offers it out and takes the first yes — so a late cancellation doesn't leave a therapist idle.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Human handoff</strong>Anything clinical, anything about a specific plan of care or authorisation goes to your team with a summary of the conversation.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">Who it's built for</div>
  <h2>However the clinic is set up</h2>
  <p class="lede">Referral-driven and cash-based clinics have very different front desks, and the receptionist is configured to match rather than assuming one shape.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Outpatient ortho &amp; sports</strong>Referral volume arrives in bursts and gets stale fast. Speed to first appointment is the whole competition.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Cash-based &amp; direct access</strong>More pricing and "do I need a referral" questions up front, answered from what you've published rather than guessed at.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Post-op rehab</strong>Surgeons want therapy started inside a window. A call that waits two days for a callback is a problem for everyone involved.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Solo &amp; small practices</strong>The owner treats and runs the desk. Every call taken during a session is a session interrupted.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Multi-location clinics</strong>Two front desks, or one covering both. Calls get captured with the location the patient actually wants.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Clinics that are moving or expanding</strong>New address, new phones, a surge of calls, and a team already stretched by the move itself.</div>
  </div>
</section>

